{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-3240"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of games and toys"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "3240"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :games-and-toys/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :materials-safety :consumer-protection :child-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :toys-games-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "ToysGamesAdvisor ⊣ Toys & Games Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A games-and-toys
 PLANT OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for injection-molding/assembly/
 safety-test lines producing finished plastic/wooden toys, board
 games, and puzzles -- not direct molding/assembly-line-equipment
 control authority and not a toy-safety-certification (e.g. ASTM
 F963 / EN 71) authority. Four ops (`:log-production-batch` /
 `:schedule-maintenance` / `:flag-safety-concern` /
 `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect :propose` only. Thirteen
 concrete governor checks elaborate this blueprint's four HARD
 invariants: propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed
 proposal-effect allowlist (no direct molding/assembly-line-equipment
 control), permanent equipment-actuate block, permanent
 toy-safety-certification-authority block (this actor never
 self-issues an ASTM F963 / EN 71 toy-safety compliance
 certification), independent plant-equipment verification/
 registration before maintenance scheduling, independent batch
 verification/registration before shipment coordination, independent
 shipment-quantity recompute against the batch's own logged
 production quantity, double-schedule guard, product-type validation,
 safety-test-pass-percent plausibility validation (choking-hazard/
 small-parts/lead-paint/phthalate testing), batch-weight plausibility
 validation, and defect-rate plausibility validation. Safety-concern
 flagging (choking-hazard, materials-safety -- lead paint, phthalate
 -- or small-parts concern) ALWAYS escalates to a human plant
 supervisor; `:log-production-batch` is the only op eligible to
 auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
